+## Common TX marker for two PPK2 instruments
+
+`RAT_GPO0` is routed through `RFC_GPO2` to DIO17. It is high during the
+RF-core transmission interval; it is not a CPU-generated pulse around a UART
+command. The mapping is reapplied in `RF_Params.pPowerCb` after each RF setup
+completes, preserving GPO0/1/3. Init and RF powerdown switch DIO17 back to a
+LOW GPIO. This also covers sleep/wake and profile changes. SDK 8.33.00.16
+actually invokes `pPowerCb`; its declared newer PowerUpFinished client event
+is not dispatched by the included multimode driver implementation.
+
+The read-only capability query is:
+
+```text
+AT+TXMARKER?
++TXMARKER:DIO=17,SOURCE=RAT_GPO0,ACTIVE=HIGH
+OK
+```
+
+This reports firmware configuration, not electrical validation of the wire.
+For the common-marker measurement, only the transmitting radio needs 0.3.1;
+the receiving radio may retain 0.3.0 and its normal UART delivery report.
+
+Connect TX DIO17 to **D0 on both PPK2 logic ports**. Connect the logic-port
+grounds to the common signal ground and both logic-port VCC references to
+the marker's **3.3 V logic reference**. Keep the two measured DUT supply paths
+separate; do not bridge the PPK VOUT rails. Logic-port VCC is the digital
+reference connection, not a replacement for the DUT supply path.
+
+The profiler integrates each current trace between its locally sampled
+rising/falling edges of the same TX pulse. The PPK clocks remain independent.
+This defines module energy over a common transmission interval; reception is
+confirmed separately over UART. It does not isolate internal receiver circuits
+or include post-reception processing outside the marker interval.
+
+Before accepting measurements, verify a complete pulse on both PPKs, agreement
+of durations, successful delivery, and repeatability across idle gaps and
+sleep/wake. A missing/ambiguous pulse must fail analysis, not fall back to a
+modeled window. All seven PHY configurations compile, but marker operation
+across those PHYs and all power levels remains a bench validation task.
+
+Build from the workspace root:
+
+```powershell
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\build-e79-at-modem.ps1 -UartPinout CH340
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\build-e79-at-modem.ps1 -UartPinout ESP32
+```
+
+The build checks generated UART pin assignments and saves versioned images,
+ELF/map, generated pin definitions and SHA-256 metadata in
+`firmware/e79_at_modem/artifacts/0.3.1/ch340_1000000` or `esp32_1000000`.
+Choose the matching image explicitly when flashing; the generic `gcc` output
+contains whichever variant was built last. The CH340 SysConfig overlay is
+derived anew from the canonical configuration on each build.
 
